A||||10||mark harmon||Sail window mounting type?||||1||
Z||000000||mark harmon||08-25-2000||08:21 AM||||I just got a set of junkyard sail windows from ebay. They look great and I was excited to finally replaced my cracked ones. This is until I pulled one off and compared it to the new ones. Seems the new ones use bolts and nuts to mount whereas mine use 2 plastic and 1 metal clip. Anyone have any input into why the difference and maybe some suggestions on how to mount the new ones. Everything lines up, but I'm not sure how to get to the backside of the windows to attach nuts.<P>Thanks, Mark||||reg||1
Z||000001||Monkeyman||08-25-2000||08:28 AM||||'84s used nuts/bolts.  '85s on up used one bolt and two plastic Christmas tree clips in the rear.  Also, the '84s were glass with a slightly different surround whereas the '85s and up were plastic.||||reg||1
Z||000002||mark harmon||08-25-2000||08:50 AM||||Anyone have pointers/shortcuts on how to install the new windows?||||reg||1
Z||000003||Oreif||08-25-2000||11:33 AM||||You need to get the metal clip from an 84 to bolt them up. I removed mine from my 86 SE and installed 84 SE glass ones. The glass ones use totally different clips that mount in the same spots as the plastic ones. I got my parts to mount it and the glass ones from Twin Lakes Fiero. I'm sure if you call Bob he'd send you a clip set for $5.00 or less.<BR>His # is 217-379-9140.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000004||mark harmon||08-25-2000||02:31 PM||||Well a trip to the boneyard answered my question to some degree and confirmed what I was told in the forum. I found an 85 that had a combination of the 84 and 86 mounting system. The 2 back screws mated with 2 metal clips that attached to the car body and the from screw on the 85 was replaced with a metal clip that was bolted to the car and snapped onto the back of the window like my 86. I grab 6 of the clips for 1.00 (couple extras). I hope to mount the 2 back screws with the metal clips and cut the front screw off the 84 windows and use the already mounted metal clip. Figures are crossed...that it works!||||reg||1
Z||000005||286SE'S||08-25-2000||06:08 PM||||Before you cut off the bolt of the 84 glass panel you may want to just install it using that bolt. The glass panels are heavy, easily twice that of the plastic one.<BR>If you remove the seat belt upper pivot bolt and a screw just above the lock striker you can pull the interior B pillar trim back and get access to the hole that the nut is hidden in.<BR>It is a 10 or 13mm  and you need a deep socket to remove it.<BR>Using the bolt will make a very secure installation as it is attached to a metal plate in the panel frame. The Clip for the plastic panel is not going to attach tight to the body and you may have it rip off at a high speed. I hope you will consider this.<BR>Terry<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000006||Oreif||08-25-2000||07:40 PM||||Don't cut the bolt!! You need to access the nut from the inside. If you cut the bolt it will not hold the glass sail panel correctly.||||reg||4
Z||000007||mark harmon||08-28-2000||09:49 AM||||It's over! The windows are in and look great. I used all the bolts after all. The 84 and 85+ window frames are different and there was no place to attach the metal bracket to the 84's. <P>I was very surprised at how easy it was to install the new windows. For those who are considering it. I pulled off the old windows, unbolted the metal clip that held the front part of the window, took out 1 screw and the upper seatbelt bolt to loosen up the plastic molding piece on the inside. I inserted the 2 metal clips that I got from the junkyard that hold the 2 rear bolts. They held better then the original plastic ones. I taped a 10mm nut and washer to a socket. Didn't want to loose them when I inserted them into the pillar. Insert the socket into the access hole from the inside and a couple twists...DONE! The first window took a little longer because of some experimentation, but the second one took about 20 minutes to complete without any frustration. <P>Thanks to all for the info! It's great to have a source like this for bouncing ideas and tracking down info!||||reg||7
Z||000008||Monkeyman||08-28-2000||07:43 PM||||Wait a minute!  The '85 setup <I>isn't</I> the same as the '86 and up???  I've sucessfully removed the sail panels from the Monkeymobile ('86 SC---moment of silence, please:::::::::::::::::::OK, carry on) and figured that the Grape Ape would be the same.  No?  How is an '85 put together?<P>------------------<BR>Dave-<BR>Grape Ape ('85GT)||||reg||1
Z||000009||Phil||08-28-2000||09:51 PM||||Monkey <BR>You can relax, my 85GT has the exact same setup as my Formula.||||reg||1
Z||000010||Monkeyman||08-28-2000||11:43 PM||||:::wiping sweat from brow:::<P>Thanx, Phil.||||reg||1
